-- הסכם קיבוצי כללי מיום 17.5.2012 — מסגרת עלות תוספת השכר, הרשויות
-- המקומיות: the general collective agreement between the Centre of Local
-- Government (for its member authorities save the three large cities), the
-- three large cities, the Centre of Regional Councils and the fire-services
-- city unions, and the New General Histadrut (its trade-union division, the
-- Ma'of union and the academics' union in מח"ר). It allocates, for the
-- local authorities' administrative and מח"ר scales, the cost frame of the
-- public-sector framework of 12.1.2011 as amended on 11.4.2011 ("הסכם
-- המסגרת", 7.25% for 1.1.2009–31.12.2012, both imported): whom it covers
-- (§2); "תוספת 2011" at 3.75% from 1.1.2012, 5.25% from 1.1.2013 and 6.25%
-- from 1.7.2013 in place of the framework's (§3); the Ma'of supplement by
-- grade, 410 down to 70 shekels, less the "balance" of the fixed
-- supplements (§4); the graded supplement, 235 down to 45 shekels (§5); the
-- assistants' supplement, 10% of the combined salary, for the kindergarten
-- and class assistants (§6); the management supplement of 5%, 7.5% and 10%
-- for the new employees in management (§7); havraa days kept at 2011's
-- (§8); the minimum wage, the exhaustion of the frame and of the claims over
-- the Ofek Hadash reform, industrial peace and 0.075% off the next frame
-- (§9); the follow-up committee (§10).
--
-- Whom it covers, and the teachers: the takanon reaches the teachers the
-- local authorities employ, and this agreement does not — it reaches the
-- administrative and מח"ר scales the Histadrut represents (§2(א); the
-- Collective Agreements Law §16, imported), and a teacher is graded in the
-- teaching scale and represented by הסתדרות המורים or ארגון המורים. It
-- names nothing of a teacher's own: it leaves out the youth, society and
-- community education scale paid by that scale's tables (§2(ב)(3)); it pays
-- the assistants who work beside kindergarten teachers and in classes a
-- supplement "in addition to" what the Ofek Hadash reform pays the
-- kindergarten assistants (§6(ב)(3); that agreement of 21.10.2010 is
-- outside the corpus); and it settles, for its own employees, every claim
-- arising from the reform and keeps industrial peace over it (recital,
-- §9(ו), §9(ח)(1)). The teachers' 2011 round — the Ofek Hadash agreements of
-- 25.1.2011, 29.2.2012 (§92), 15.4.2013 and 22.7.2013 — is held against
-- this agreement's "תוספת 2011" month by month in
-- l4/tests/2012-02-29_ofek-hadash_amendment_hascam-hashlama-tests.l4. The
-- salary grids it attaches "for convenience" as annexes א' and ב' are not
-- in the corpus. It speaks to no pay item of l4/lib/vocabulary.l4 and is
-- in no root.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT collective_agreements_law
IMPORT `2008-04-17_framework-agreement_public-sector`
IMPORT `2011-01-12_framework-agreement_public-sector_tosefet-2011`
IMPORT `2011-04-11_framework-agreement_public-sector_amendment`

§ `הסכם קיבוצי כללי — מסגרת עלות תוספת השכר, הרשויות המקומיות (17.5.2012)`

DECLARE `local-government action of 17.5.2012` IS ONE OF
    `pay the Ma'of supplement from the October 2012 salary`
    `pay the graded supplement from the October 2012 salary`
    `pay the assistants' supplement from the October 2012 salary`
    `pay the management supplement from the October 2012 salary`
    `define the management levels unanimously by 1.9.2012`
    `strike or harm the work over the Ofek Hadash reform`
    `strike or harm the work over this agreement's matters before 1.1.2013`
    `follow the agreement of 17.5.2012 and decide its disputes unanimously`
    `discuss an undecided dispute of 17.5.2012 with the wages commissioner`
    `go to the courts over an undecided dispute of 17.5.2012`

